nding, the network normally makes handover decisions based on the measurement event. The measurement results within TTT may include both actual results and predicted results. Thus, it is not useful if the UE reports the latest result is from actual measurement or prediction. Observation 11: The UE only reports one measurement result (either actual result or prediction result) for each cell, so the network does not have different strategies for the two cases. Proposal 13: For temporal domain case B, no need to differentiate prediction results or actual results. The content of measurement report In the existing spec, the measurement report can include: The measurement results for each serving cell configured with servingCellMO; For each MeasObjectId referenced in the measIdList which is also referenced with servingCellMO, other than the measObjectId corresponding with the measId that triggered the measurement reporting, the measurement results of best neighbor cell (if configured and available). For the MO corresponding with the measId that triggered the measurement report, the measurement results for the best cells up to maxReportCells. For the content of the measurement report, we need to consider whether the UE reports the same content for one cell when the cell is associated with the measId that triggers the measurement report, and when it is not associated with that measId. Taking the following figure as example, If both MeasId 1 and MeasId 2 are configured with temporal domain case A, if MeasId 1 triggers the measurement reporting, the measurement report includes: For PCell: the actual measurement results and multiple prediction results within PW; For SCell 1: Option 1: the actual measurement results and multiple prediction results within PW; Option 2: actual measu

